Srinitha's contribution to the project: I conducted several hours of research on similar initiatives, including the UCLA sign language translation glove and haptic ASL technologies discussed in articles like Deaf Vibes, to inform our focus on tactile correction for handshapes. I also looked into the hardware details by studying the flex sensors, IMU wiring architecture, ESP32 microcontroller functionalities, and the provided schematic, while also experimenting with PCB prototyping in KiCad to explore custom board designs. On the software front, I developed the Flutter-based mobile app UI, integrating it seamlessly with the Firebase database for performance tracking, implementing push notifications, and setting up user authentication via the console. Additionally, I assisted in establishing stable BLE connections for real-time sensor data streaming from the glove to the app, and gained foundational knowledge on electronics components such as resistors and voltage dividers to support hardware troubleshooting.
